    "done_when": "The project layer of flight config accepts a review.suite block, holding a command as an argv list run from the checkout root and a budget such as 20m. The block is declared in reckon/_flight_schema.py, regenerated into docs/_shared/flight.schema.json with scripts/regen_flight_schema.py, and read by a function in reckon/flight.py. That function returns None when nothing is declared and refuses a malformed block by name. docs/state/reckon/flight.yaml declares reckon's suite as the root .venv python running pytest -n 8 -p no:cacheprovider -q over tests/, with a budget of 20m.\n\nA new module, reckon/crew/standing_suite.py, provides three functions:\n- run: runs the declared command under its budget, killing the whole process group at the budget, and captures the log to a caller-named path. It returns a record carrying revision, command, exit_status, collected, passed, failed, errored, duration_seconds, budget_seconds, collection_failed, over_budget, log_path and observed_at. The counts are parsed from the log, covering both the plain \"collected N items\" form and the pytest-xdist \"[N items]\" form. The FAILED and ERROR ids and the result-count tokens are read with the parsers that already exist in reckon/crew/review.py and reckon/crew/promotion.py, imported rather than copied, and neither file is edited.\n- record: writes one JSON file per run under the project state directory (docs/state/reckon/suite-runs/ for this repository; the directory is resolved from the project root and name the caller passes), through a writer that already exists in reckon/_store.py.\n- hold_reason(project_root, tier): returns a sentence naming the revision, observed_at, and whether the run failed to collect or overran its budget. It does so only for tier none or light, and only while the latest record failed either way and no later lead waiver record exists. Otherwise it returns None. A waiver is written by a record_waiver function, carrying who and why.\n\nPromotion is not wired in this node. tests/test_standing_suite.py builds throwaway projects under tmp_path and runs each with sys.executable -m pytest, writing nothing outside tmp_path. It covers:\n- a suite with a syntax error, which records collection_failed and holds tier none and light but not full;\n- a later passing run, which lifts the hold;\n- a sleep past a one-second budget, which records over_budget, and whose process group is gone afterwards;\n- a waiver, which lifts the hold;\n- the flight reader, returning None when undeclared and refusing a malformed block.\n\nThe file passes at exit 0, together with tests/test_flight.py. The manifest records base and head arms in the armed JSON form with their FAILED ids, and the head arm runs at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the collection-failure hold case is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The full project suite is not run by this node.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "A project declares its own suite command and whole-run budget, a runner records each run's counts at a named revision, and a hold function says when tier none and light promotions must wait",
